===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# The [[expression]] of [[gratitude]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1769|author={{w|Firishta}}|tlr={{w|Alexander Dow}}|title=Tales translated from the Persian of Inatulla of Delhi|volume=I|publisher=P. and W. Wilson et al.|location=Dublin|page=3|text=Now the happy king laid the forehead of '''thankſgiving''' upon the duſt of gratitude; he opened the doors of his wealth to the four winds, and enriched the world, at once, with his munificence.}}
#* {{RQ:Burroughs Land That Time Forgot||IV|passage=The waters grew suddenly lighter, and my spirits rose accordingly. I shouted down to those below that I saw daylight ahead, and a great shout of '''thanksgiving''' reverberated through the ship. A moment later we emerged into sunlit water, and immediately I raised the periscope and looked about me upon the strangest landscape I had ever seen.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=08 Dec 79|volume=7|number=20|journal=Gay Community News|page=1|title=Services Honor Milk, Moscone|quotee=Dianne Feinstein|text=People gathered, she said, "not simply in an attitude of mourning, grievous as those events were, but rather in the spirit of '''thanksgiving''' that George and Harvey were among us, that they shared with us their dreams and aspirations for the San Francisco of the 1980s."}}
# A short [[prayer]] said at [[meal]]s; [[grace]], a [[benediction]].
# A public [[celebration]] in [[acknowledgement]] of [[divine]] [[favour]].
#* {{RQ:Bindloss Dust of Conflict|chapter=20|passage=Hester Earle and Violet Wayne were moving about the aisle with bundles of wheat-ears and streamers of ivy, for the harvest '''thanksgiving''' was shortly to be celebrated, while the vicar stood waiting for their directions on the chancel steps with a great handful of crimson gladioli.}}

